From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:26:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] v4l2: skip the dma-buf CPU sync when the MDP hardware
 path is taken

decodedTiled->syncStartRead()/syncEndRead() bracket the whole
serviceDeviceTask detile step since the original CPU-only libyuv
path (before MDP existed): they call DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC(START|READ)
and (END|READ) on the ~3 MiB tiled VDEC output buffer so the CPU
sees the hardware decoders writes before libyuv reads them with
its own pointer.

MdpImageConverter::convertMM21ToNV12 never touches TiledMM21Image::y
or ::uv, only ::dmaBufFd: MDP is a second hardware DMA engine, not
the CPU, reading the same buffer the VDEC wrote. Device-to-device
coherency for that transfer is established by the kernels own
dma_buf_attach()/dma_buf_map_attachment() inside translate_fd(),
independent of this ioctl, which exists solely for CPU access.
e2ea453 (23.09, first MDP convereter) kept the pre-existing sync
call wrapping the new combined primary+fallback call without
reconsidering it, so every MDP-converted frame has been paying for
a CPU cache invalidate+flush pass over the whole tiled buffer that
no one reads.

serviceDeviceTask now tries the MDP path first with fallbackConverter
= nullptr and no surrounding sync; only if that returns false
(mMdpImageConverter absent, permanently disabled, or a real runtime
failure) does it sync and retry through the CPU/libyuv path, same as
before. detileFrom/detileFrom10 themselves are unchanged.

Does not touch the two remaining open items on i-yxpnata4lxwr: the
V4L2 CAPTURE pool needs 25 buffers for 1920x1088 (driver-reported,
not something this HAL controls) which combined with the surface
BufferQueues own slot count touches 46 distinct dma_bufs per 150
frame session per dmesg (mdp_ioctl_free_iova_cache_by_node), so a
real fraction of frames still pay a cold iova-cache miss in
translate_fd regardless of this patch; and serviceDeviceTask runs
decode dequeue and convert on the same SequencedTaskRunner with no
overlap between decoding frame N+1 and converting frame N. Both need
a device measurement to size.
---
 v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
index 7dab6b2..4e19229 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
@@ -697,10 +697,10 @@ void V4L2Decoder::serviceDeviceTask(bool event) {
                 return;
             }
 
-            decodedTiled->syncStartRead();
             bool detiled;
             bool primaryFailed = false;
             if (mCaptureIsMt10) {
+                decodedTiled->syncStartRead();
                 TiledMT10Image tiledImage;
                 tiledImage.data = decodedTiled->data();
                 tiledImage.strideY = mCaptureStrideY;
@@ -709,6 +709,7 @@ void V4L2Decoder::serviceDeviceTask(bool event) {
                 tiledImage.dmaBufSize = decodedTiled->size();
                 detiled = frame->detileFrom10(mImageConverter.get(), tiledImage,
                                               mCodedSize.width, mCodedSize.height);
+                decodedTiled->syncEndRead();
             } else {
                 TiledMM21Image tiledImage;
                 tiledImage.y = decodedTiled->data();
@@ -720,10 +721,16 @@ void V4L2Decoder::serviceDeviceTask(bool event) {
                 tiledImage.dmaBufSize = decodedTiled->size();
                 ImageConverter* const primaryConverter =
                         (mMdpImageConverter && !mMdpFailed) ? mMdpImageConverter.get() : nullptr;
-                detiled = frame->detileFrom(primaryConverter, mImageConverter.get(), tiledImage,
+                detiled = primaryConverter &&
+                          frame->detileFrom(primaryConverter, nullptr, tiledImage,
                                             mCodedSize.width, mCodedSize.height, &primaryFailed);
+                if (!detiled) {
+                    decodedTiled->syncStartRead();
+                    detiled = frame->detileFrom(nullptr, mImageConverter.get(), tiledImage,
+                                                mCodedSize.width, mCodedSize.height, nullptr);
+                    decodedTiled->syncEndRead();
+                }
             }
-            decodedTiled->syncEndRead();
 
             if (primaryFailed && !mMdpFailed) {
                 mMdpFailed = true;
